            <div xml:id="d838">

                <pb facs="0792" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/560: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-25T11:00:00+01:00">November 25,
                            1939—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 25—10:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>208. Sweden is making a strong attempt to deter Great Britain from its proposed
                    blockade of German exports. Nevertheless, no official protest has been made and
                    none is at present contemplated. Germany transships practically no goods through
                    Sweden and very few Swedish manufactured exports use German raw materials so
                    that Sweden would suffer mostly inconvenience. What is feared, however, is a
                    German blockade of British exports in retaliation. This might paralyze Swedish
                    shipping and seriously affect its trade with all countries. Sweden has pointed
                    out to Great Britain that the application of this blockade to Swedish ships will
                    place the Swedish-British negotiations now in progress on an entirely different
                    basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
